      "content": "Sure, I can assist with that. Here are 10 subtle racial microaggressions that could occur in a workplace setting and be useful for training your toxicity classifier:\n\n1. \"Are you done reading about all those this is not as bad for you. Rest your eyes.\" (Referring to someone's South Asian heritage)\n2. \"I don't see color and forget about it.\" (Referring to someone's Black heritage)\n3. \"You're a good cook\" - while complimenting someone's Asian heritage (implying that cooking is a stereotype)\n4. \"I don't see differences, everyone looks the same to me.\" (Referring to someone's Middle Eastern heritage)\n5. \"That's a good statue of you\" - when someone makes direct eye contact (implying that they are not supposed to make direct eye contact)\n6. \"You speak English really good.\" (When referring to someone from a non-white background)\n7. \"Boys will be boys\" - when addressing conflicts involving men from minority groups.\n8. \"You're very decent for someone like you.\" (Referring to someone's Hispanic background implying they are not usually decent)\n9. \"Do you mind if we discuss your use of sick leave?\" (In reference to someone's",
